  "description": "A parametric TOILET on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nBACK TO FRONT IS THE LENGTH AXIS. The cistern sits at the object's u0 edge, so the back of the WC is the back of its box: drop it on a wall segment, anchor \"Top-Center\", and it faces into the room with nothing to rotate.\n\nTHE PAN IS AN ELLIPSE, not a rectangle. A WC drawn as a box is the one sanitary symbol nobody accepts, so the pan and the seat ring are 28-point ellipse rings extruded with mprism — the same ring is the plan outline and the solid's footprint, so the two cannot disagree. Everything squarer (cistern, pedestal) stays on the shared quad-prism table.\n\nTHREE STYLES on one ternary over the cistern's base height. Close-coupled sets it on the pan at seat height; Wall-hung lifts both clear of the floor and shortens the pedestal to a bracket; Floor-mounted runs it to the floor. One flow, not three.\n\nCLEARANCE IS PUBLISHED RATHER THAN DRAWN. 600 mm in front is what most codes want, and it scales with the object, so a fitted plan can check it without a second node.",
